      "text": "To solve the problem, we will use the relationship between pressure and volume given by Boyle's Law, which states that the pressure of a given mass of gas is inversely proportional to its volume at constant temperature. Mathematically, this can be expressed as:\n\n\\[ P_1 V_1 = P_2 V_2 \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( P_1 \\) is the initial pressure,\n- \\( V_1 \\) is the initial volume,\n- \\( P_2 \\) is the final pressure,\n- \\( V_2 \\) is the final volume.\n\nGiven:\n- \\( P_1 = 5 \\) kPa,\n- \\( V_1 = 2.28 \\) liters,\n- \\( V_2 = 5.7 \\) liters.\n\nWe need to find \\( P_2 \\). Rearranging Boyle's Law to solve for \\( P_2 \\), we get:\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{P_1 V_1}{V_2} \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values into the equation:\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\times 2.28 \\, \\text{liters}}{5.7 \\, \\text{liters}} \\]\n\nNow, perform the multiplication and division:\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{11.4 \\, \\text{kPa} \\cdot \\text{liters}}{5.7 \\, \\text{liters}} \\]\n\n\\[ P_2 \\approx 1.986957 \\, \\text{kPa} \\]\n\nRounding to three decimal places, the new pressure is:\n\n\\[ P_2 \\approx 1.987 \\, \\text{kPa} \\]\n\nThus, the new pressure in the 5.7 liter container is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1.987}\n\\]",
