      "text": "To solve the problem, we can use the concept of inverse proportionality between pressure and volume for a constant temperature. According to Boyle's Law, which is a special case of Charles's Law for constant volume and given constant temperature, the product of pressure and volume is constant. Mathematically, this can be represented as:\n\n\\[ P_1 V_1 = P_2 V_2 \\]\n\nGiven:\n- Initial volume \\( V_1 = 2.28 \\) liters\n- Initial pressure \\( P_1 = 5 \\) kPa\n- Final volume \\( V_2 = 5.7 \\) liters\n- Final pressure \\( P_2 \\) (which we need to find)\n\nFirst, we will use the formula to solve for \\( P_2 \\):\n\n\\[ P_1 V_1 = P_2 V_2 \\]\n\nSubstitute the given values:\n\n\\[ 5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\times 2.28 \\, \\text{liters} = P_2 \\times 5.7 \\, \\text{liters} \\]\n\nNow, solve for \\( P_2 \\):\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\times 2.28 \\, \\text{liters}}{5.7 \\, \\text{liters}} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\r\nP1 = 5  # kPa\r\nV1 = 2.28  # liters\r\nV2 = 5.7  # liters\r\n\r\n# Using the formula P1 * V1 = P2 * V2 to solve for P2\r\nP2 = (P1 * V1) / V2\r\nprint(P2)\n```\n```output\n2.0\n```\nThe new pressure \\( P_2 \\) after the oxygen is moved to a 5.7-liter container at the same temperature is \\(\\boxed{2.0}\\) kPa.",
